# Vulnerabilities deliberately accepted, with the reason and who decided.
#
# This file is for findings that HAVE a fix but that we are choosing not to take
# yet. Findings with no fix available are already excluded by the scan itself
# (`--ignore-unfixed`), so they do not belong here -- there is nothing to accept
# or decline.
#
# Format: one vulnerability id per line. Always leave a comment above it saying
# what the exposure actually is and when to revisit, otherwise this file quietly
# turns into a place where problems go to be forgotten.
#
# Currently empty. For the record, the findings the scan drops as unfixable:
#
#   CVE-2025-71329, CVE-2025-71330 -- image-size 0.7.5, denial of service when
#   parsing a malformed ICNS/JXL/HEIF image. No fixed version exists. It reaches
#   us four levels deep under deck.gl (deck.gl -> @loaders.gl/textures ->
#   texture-compressor -> image-size), where texture-compressor is a build-time
#   GPU-texture CLI that the app never calls at runtime. npm's suggested "fix"
#   is to downgrade deck.gl from 9.x to 8.9.36, which would be a far larger
#   change than the exposure warrants. Revisit if deck.gl 9.x ever refreshes its
#   pinned @loaders.gl.
